WEBVTT

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:48.880
<v Speaker 2>Overcome the difficulties and how and why difficult like they could overcome breakfast specificity show.

00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:56.799
<v Speaker 2>It's really all about transition to everyone who wants to expand it and what they did to get there.

00:00:56.799 --> 00:01:07.439
<v Speaker 2>As such, while the focus is on LGBTQ journeys, I want to share the stories of all people who have found their way to success.

00:01:07.439 --> 00:01:26.000
<v Speaker 2>My hope is to have this platform for all of us to be together while listening to successful stories, amazing life experiences, inspirational journeys, as well as having good laughs and lots of smiles.

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:34.000
<v Speaker>Ladies and gentlemen, may I introduce you to something quite extraordinary?

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:37.200
<v Speaker>It's the Breakfast with Tiffany Show podcast.

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:43.920
<v Speaker>And now it is with great pleasure that I introduce you to your host, Tiffany Rossdale.

00:01:45.519 --> 00:01:47.280
<v Speaker 2>Welcome to Breakfast with Tiffany Show.

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:53.200
<v Speaker 2>I'm your host, Tiffany Rossdale, and we're back on another episode of the show.

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:58.000
<v Speaker 2>And today we have not just one, but two amazing guests on the show.

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:11.199
<v Speaker 2>And today's episode is very, very special because we are joined by two remarkable storytellers whose work has quietly reshaped the landscape of queer cinema in Asia.

00:02:11.199 --> 00:02:23.759
<v Speaker 2>Our first guest is Ray Jung, an acclaimed Hong Kong filmmaker and screenwriter known for telling LGBTQ stories with rare sensitivity, honesty, and restraint.

00:02:23.759 --> 00:02:40.080
<v Speaker 2>A former lawyer-turned filmmaker, Ray later earned his MFA from Columbia University and has since built a body of work that centers emotional truth over spectacle and humanity over headlines.

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:51.759
<v Speaker 2>His films have given visibility to queer lives often left unseen, especially older LGBTQ communities navigating love, family, and societal silence.

00:02:51.759 --> 00:02:59.680
<v Speaker 2>His widely celebrated features, Suk Suk, Twilight's Kiss, touch audiences around the world.

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:12.800
<v Speaker 2>And his latest film, All Shall Be Well, premiered at the Berlinal Panorama, where it won the prestigious Teddy Award, one of the highest honors in queer cinema.

00:03:12.800 --> 00:03:24.800
<v Speaker 2>And joining him today is Patra Ow, an extraordinary actress whose performances have become deeply intertwined with Ray's cinematic universe.

00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:38.560
<v Speaker 2>Patra is a central figure in All Shall Be Well, where her portrayal of a woman confronting love, loss, and legal invisibility is both devastating and quietly powerful.

00:03:38.560 --> 00:03:47.599
<v Speaker 2>Patra brings her rare emotional precision to the screen, embodying characters with restraint, dignity, and profound inner life.

00:03:47.599 --> 00:04:03.120
